# Shared API

Read root `AGENTS.md` and `docs/API_ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing this folder.

- Keep `@/shared/api` as the application's import facade; app code must not import
  `@mithra/api-client` directly.
- The files `client.ts`, `errors.ts`, `tokens.ts`, and `types.ts` are thin package re-exports.
  Transport logic belongs in `packages/api-client/src/client/`.
- Current app services call raw package transport primitives. Package domain services are parallel;
  do not silently migrate or create a third service path during a feature.
- Preserve explicit demo/live behavior with `isLiveApi()`. Never let an unsupported mode fail as an
  unexplained blank screen.
- Map reusable wire-format differences in `mappers/`, not in pages.
- The backend OpenAPI document is authoritative. Do not invent an endpoint or payload; record a
  backend gap when the contract is insufficient.
- Do not edit `openapi.json` or `schema.d.ts` manually.
- Use `getErrorMessage()` for UI errors. Remember that `assertApiSuccess` can reject an HTTP 200
  envelope whose `success` field is false.
